@* The offline shell: the one document the service worker stores and the one it serves when a navigation into the
   authenticated surface finds no network. It is anonymous and static on purpose. A stored document is replayed to whoever
   launches the installed application next, so it carries no user, no tenant, no antiforgery token and no policy nonce, and
   HostShell.ApplyPageHeadersAsync is what serves it storable instead of no-store. The address the browser asked for is kept,
   so a reload retries the page the user was on rather than starting over. *@
@page "/app/offline"
@using Blazor.Client.Shell
@using Blazor.Host.Shell
@attribute [OfflineShellPage]
@layout StaticPageLayout

<PageTitle>@CommonStrings.YouAreOffline</PageTitle>

<OfflineContent/>
